---
title: Command-line reference
order: 60
tags: [reference, cli]
---

Every command takes a documentation root or a build directory and returns a
zero exit code on success.

## build

```
quaydoc build [ROOT] [-o OUT] [--archive PATH]
```

Render the tree at `ROOT` (default `.`) into `OUT` (default the configured
`output_dir`). With `--archive PATH` the output is also bundled into a gzip
tar.

## check

```
quaydoc check [OUTDIR]
```

Run the integrity checks described in [[Links and references]] over a built
site. The exit code is nonzero when any error-level issue is found, and a
`.quay-check.txt` report is written into the build directory.

## serve

```
quaydoc serve [OUTDIR] [--port PORT] [--host HOST]
```

Serve `OUTDIR` (default `site`) over HTTP. The default host is
`127.0.0.1` and the default port is `8000`.

## watch

```
quaydoc watch [ROOT]
```

Rebuild the site at `ROOT` whenever a source file changes, until
interrupted.

## search

```
quaydoc search TERMS... [OUTDIR]
```

Query the `search_index.json` of a built site and print matching page URLs
in rank order.

## init

```
quaydoc init [ROOT]
```

Scaffold a documentation tree: a `quaydoc.toml` and an `index.qd`.
